  "id": "Compound::DB00448 - Gene::1562",
  "verbalization": "Lansoprazole is implicated in the activation of Cyp2c18 through a shared pathway involving Omeprazole, a proton pump inhibitor. The evidence suggests that Lansoprazole causes an increase in blood gastrin, which is then mediated by Omeprazole, and both substances bind to Cyp2c18. This indicates a potential mechanism by which Lansoprazole indirectly influences Cyp2c18 activity, likely through the metabolic effects of Omeprazole. The recurring connection between Lansoprazole and Omeprazole, both belonging to the benzimidazole class and proton pump inhibitors, supports a common pharmacological context. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible dependency on the metabolic activation of Omeprazole to modulate Cyp2c18, suggesting a broader role for this enzyme in the systemic effects of these drugs.",
